++
++## Who should buy it
++
++- **Video editors and colorists** who regularly receive low-res or archival source material.
++- **AI content creators** who generate video with tools like Higgsfield, Kling, or Veo and need a consistent upscaling step in their pipeline.
++- **Family archivists** digitizing and restoring old home video or photos — a one-time project that doesn't justify a subscription.
++- **Photographers** delivering large-format prints from files that need a resolution boost.
++
++## Who should skip it
++
++- Anyone whose source material is already high-resolution for its intended output.
++- Anyone who needs upscaling for a single one-off image or clip — a free or cheap online upscaler may cover that without the full purchase.
++- Anyone expecting upscaling to fix genuinely unusable footage (extreme blur, very low bitrate compression) — it improves, it doesn't perform magic.
